# tests/BUDGET - caps test-code growth (scripts/test-budget.sh, docs/procedures/tests.md "Test audit").
# Lines, one per field; blank lines and # comments are ignored.
#   paths: <space-separated globs>   the test files counted (git pathspec globs, relative to the
#                                    repository root; tracked and untracked files both count).
#                                    A project edits this for its own suites.
#   ceiling: <N>                     non-blank test lines the suite holds today.
#   allowance: <N>                   net new lines a change may add above the ceiling with no record.
#   raise: <old>-><new> <YYYY-MM-DD> <reason>
#                                    one per ceiling increase, oldest first, reason required. To pass
#                                    a larger addition, set ceiling: to the new count in the same
#                                    change and add the raise line.
# `check` fails when the count exceeds ceiling + allowance. Deleting or consolidating duplicate
# tests lowers the count; lower ceiling: to the new count when a pass has removed lines.
paths: tests/template/*.sh tests/template/fixtures/*
ceiling: 11058
allowance: 400
